## The Minimal Model

- There are \(m+2\) centered latent source slots \(S_0,\ldots,S_{m+1}\).
- Independence makes cumulants add across source slots.
- Finite \(K\)-th moments make cumulants through order \(K\) well-defined.
- Non-Gaussianity supplies higher-order information beyond covariance.
- Genericity means distinct finite loading slopes, nonzero direct slope, and nonzero retained source cumulants.

@formal ass:independent-sources

---

## The Two Axis Conventions

- In the forward convention, the direct slot has loading direction \((1,\gamma)\), the middle slots have \((1,\rho_j)\), and the fixed vertical slot has \((0,1)\).
- In the reverse convention, the fixed horizontal slot has \((1,0)\), the middle slots have \((\sigma_j,1)\), and the direct slot has \((\delta,1)\).
- The axis normalization makes the two representations directly comparable.
- In the running example, the normalization says which latent shock slot is treated as the direct recursive component.

@formal ass:forward-axis-model

@formal ass:reverse-axis-model

