## Where the Literature Stands

- Structural causal models and graphical identification give the broad language for observational direction questions.
- LiNGAM and ICA show how non-Gaussianity can identify linear structure under stronger source restrictions.
- Latent-variable LiNGAM work studies how hidden confounding changes what can be recovered.
- Recent cumulant and tensor methods use higher-order restrictions to recover latent causal information.
- The immediate comparator proves a direction test under an arbitrary number of latent confounders, using an order-\(2m+3\) rank-deficiency construction.
- This paper gives an algebraic representation-level separation result at order \(2m+2\), with a sharper real generic separation order for \(m\ge3\).

