## Main Result 4: The Real Order Improves

- The information order \(K^\star(m)\) is the smallest truncation order at which, for each arrow and outside a proper real algebraic subset, a real feasible cumulant vector has no representation under the opposite arrow.

@informal thm:improved-real-information-order: For \(m\ge3\), order \(2m+1\) is enough for generic real opposite-arrow exclusion, and \(K^\star(m)\) is at most \(2m+1\).

@formal thm:improved-real-information-order

